-- The whole video for video dictation: every sentence of the video's own English captions, not only the eight chosen
-- when the videos were added (2804 sentences more, over 30 videos).
--
-- Sentences and times come from the videos' human-made English captions, the way V9 did them: a sentence starts at the
-- caption cue where it begins and ends where it finishes (+100 ms, never past the next sentence's start), spread over
-- the words of a cue by letter count, so a time can be off by a fraction of a second inside a long cue. Left out are
-- sentences that cannot be dictated well: under 3 or over 32 words, with digits (a number is typed
-- one way and said another), spoken labels or capitals only, web addresses, a caption slip or a sound written out as a
-- word (ahhhh, occassion), or shorter than a second. A sentence of more than
-- 26 words is cut at its commas into pieces. A caption typo in the new sentences is not corrected here.
--
-- The sentences that were already there keep their id, text and Vietnamese (so the learners' attempts and progress stay
-- valid); the new ones have no Vietnamese (translation_vi is NULL, the player then shows no "Xem nghĩa" for them).
-- Afterwards sequence_no of every touched video is renumbered by start time, with the old and new sentences mixed.
-- The five videos without a caption file at the time (jNQXAC9IVRw, UF8uR6Z6KLc, iG9CE55wbtY, qp0HIF3SfI4, wHGqp8lz36c)
-- are left as they were.

-- 1. new sentences, with a temporary number that clashes with nothing
