    ('44a120c0-51ec-5521-9fd1-0d0214db9562', 'Frq4TZf0F1s', 110, 649743, 657771, 'Repeat the phrases out loud and try to use them in real life.'),
    ('d166fff9-e393-5109-a53c-345250551589', 'Frq4TZf0F1s', 111, 657771, 663995, 'The more you practice, the more confident you will feel.'),
    ('4dc2179c-84ec-5209-aae3-86f71e0d6535', 'Frq4TZf0F1s', 112, 663995, 667622, 'Thank you for learning with me today.'),
    ('3129eccb-a9d5-5aa5-b5e4-161fa6f43b0b', 'Frq4TZf0F1s', 113, 667622, 669663, 'I''m so proud of you.'),
    ('9cf95eea-a25e-5942-9591-1d74734d2761', 'Frq4TZf0F1s', 114, 669663, 675416, 'See you in the next lesson here on English Phrases Hub.'),
    ('75cbed1e-c454-5330-a9cf-2bc8f3a35fef', 'Frq4TZf0F1s', 115, 675416, 679059, 'Bye-bye and have a wonderful day.'),
    ('7daa452c-37fc-5630-8c68-a23f55031d79', 'I_tRSrPru94', 1, 2745, 4896, 'Easy English Conversations.'),
    ('33aecf65-b495-5f27-b091-f38bb7c6ca6d', 'I_tRSrPru94', 2, 22243, 24432, 'Hello, how''s it going?'),
    ('01723e2e-2edf-5c7a-81b6-deec32120443', 'I_tRSrPru94', 3, 26995, 28158, 'What are your names?'),
    ('94a2e58a-0dcc-5c6a-a1b7-4d093129bd46', 'I_tRSrPru94', 4, 29379, 30842, 'And I''m Sian.'),
    ('5da9261a-ae43-5fe1-a397-45af497b36d4', 'I_tRSrPru94', 5, 30907, 32332, 'What''s your name?'),
    ('d65ca6ca-9753-54c4-bb69-30b8c5265566', 'I_tRSrPru94', 6, 32332, 33647, 'My name''s Georgie.'),
    ('ce8bc540-d450-5eec-ba25-fa5454666c2e', 'I_tRSrPru94', 7, 33647, 34862, 'Nice to meet you.'),
    ('838cc367-2134-59c2-b762-8021ad7421d9', 'I_tRSrPru94', 8, 34862, 36742, 'Yeah, great to meet you too.'),
    ('aaaf7017-7c0e-5621-9d5e-64adb409973d', 'I_tRSrPru94', 9, 41070, 42548, 'What''s your name?'),
    ('ca1a435f-36f5-5934-9e1c-ea75f76493ad', 'I_tRSrPru94', 10, 44041, 45454, 'What''s your name?'),
    ('fcd02381-f7df-5582-b57c-00eb672cd9c8', 'I_tRSrPru94', 11, 47447, 49276, 'Nice to meet you, Georgie!'),
    ('dca249fe-c307-5c8e-a3d2-fb4f5ec21236', 'I_tRSrPru94', 12, 53500, 55052, 'Where are they from?'),
    ('974cd480-c81f-5c2c-b375-6005c58c01c5', 'I_tRSrPru94', 13, 56552, 58601, 'And where do they live?'),
    ('c53019c0-6149-55de-8303-435a76e5b6bf', 'I_tRSrPru94', 14, 59830, 61754, 'Find out in the next video!'),
    ('d51d0527-bd12-5386-92ae-02abb42baae2', 'I_tRSrPru94', 15, 65577, 66961, 'What''s his name?'),
    ('b6414eba-dd02-53b5-8e56-1431e58f76c0', 'I_tRSrPru94', 16, 66975, 68345, 'His name''s Tim.'),
    ('9f53568b-02cd-5ff0-bd3d-112c17811107', 'I_tRSrPru94', 17, 68599, 70360, 'Lovely to meet you, Tim.'),
    ('d598f87c-dc9f-58bd-ae35-737a4827aa76', 'I_tRSrPru94', 18, 70936, 72883, 'Now, what''s her name?'),
    ('d3e2e57b-d9b2-579b-a8ed-dcabe6e173a0', 'I_tRSrPru94', 19, 72883, 74415, 'Her name''s Sian.'),
    ('dea77a5a-453d-5351-934a-3f6dc1b32689', 'I_tRSrPru94', 20, 75111, 77020, 'Oh, she''s Sian.'),
    ('8a9690b3-5b70-591f-86e5-0ed07e1755fa', 'I_tRSrPru94', 21, 78885, 80149, 'Nice to meet you.'),
    ('50a7c578-02e5-566b-9f0e-5db5abaedc6c', 'I_tRSrPru94', 22, 80149, 81776, 'Great to meet you too.'),
    ('a750de25-f527-5da5-b2b5-e6d85ef4ca5c', 'I_tRSrPru94', 23, 81776, 91105, 'So, I''m Buli, her name''s Sian, her name''s Georgie, and his name''s Tim.'),
    ('ce6e4ae6-d2fd-549a-95a1-45f20c59f5df', 'I_tRSrPru94', 24, 93534, 95287, 'What''s your name?'),
    ('23d7f528-a87f-55dd-8e75-1cc417c4c021', 'I_tRSrPru94', 25, 100413, 102107, 'Nice to meet you.'),
    ('0d6d38a1-337f-5b00-9351-6236ee72a2f6', 'I_tRSrPru94', 26, 107640, 109790, 'Her name''s Georgie.'),
    ('692ff485-8b11-5297-9547-3a613f32d8c2', 'I_tRSrPru94', 27, 112474, 114868, 'His name''s Tim.'),
    ('e8369767-814a-5deb-9a31-51df6c2816ab', 'I_tRSrPru94', 28, 115820, 117822, 'But what''s his name?'),
    ('84583037-d3f1-5eb8-8058-7a5e5d5b5b03', 'I_tRSrPru94', 29, 139904, 144903, 'Click here to learn eight different ways to say ''How are you?'''),
    ('10e063ff-2039-5f6b-998b-280e968d3f6f', 'I_tRSrPru94', 30, 144964, 148611, 'And click here to subscribe to our channel.'),
    ('41dbe3ba-df33-5f23-bf7f-51395e6a1140', 'OyK0oE5rwFY', 1, 18743, 26076, 'Your posture, the way you hold your body when you''re sitting or standing, is the foundation for every movement your body makes,'),
    ('d7ace5fe-c133-5e98-bd5f-8f6499f0fd39', 'OyK0oE5rwFY', 2, 26076, 30547, 'and can determine how well your body adapts to the stresses on it.'),
    ('05470841-451b-511b-9b84-37151c06e4ec', 'OyK0oE5rwFY', 3, 51791, 58832, 'Over time, these dysfunctional adaptations impair your body''s ability to deal with the forces on it.'),
    ('8d124b34-63fe-5522-bce7-9ef990df5b7c', 'OyK0oE5rwFY', 4, 58832, 69532, 'Poor posture inflicts extra wear and tear on your joints and ligaments, increases the likelihood of accidents, and makes some organs, like your lungs, less efficient.'),
    ('cdf54323-1f97-568d-9630-77e8f5a5d336', 'OyK0oE5rwFY', 5, 69532, 78610, 'Researchers have linked poor posture to scoliosis, tension headaches, and back pain, though it isn''t the exclusive cause of any of them.'),
    ('582f7008-ae4e-5f0f-9bd2-e994568b3dec', 'OyK0oE5rwFY', 6, 78610, 83947, 'Posture can even influence your emotional state and your sensitivity to pain.'),
    ('02ce4906-7e0c-512c-8d8a-e2af954fec52', 'OyK0oE5rwFY', 7, 83947, 87731, 'So there are a lot of reasons to aim for good posture.'),
    ('d734762a-9f0c-5238-b162-c300a98797d3', 'OyK0oE5rwFY', 8, 87731, 89593, 'But it''s getting harder these days.'),
    ('322058de-495b-5f8b-872a-cefe206f7bda', 'OyK0oE5rwFY', 9, 89593, 96954, 'Sitting in an awkward position for a long time can promote poor posture, and so can using computers or mobile devices,'),
    ('915bd5d5-d383-5769-be46-c04159c2ec39', 'OyK0oE5rwFY', 10, 96954, 99229, 'which encourage you to look downward.'),
    ('d4504a39-dbaf-5d80-aa49-d6e72bdd004b', 'OyK0oE5rwFY', 11, 99229, 103823, 'Many studies suggest that, on average, posture is getting worse.'),
    ('7d41014e-c589-52cd-a025-27794296425c', 'OyK0oE5rwFY', 12, 103823, 106347, 'So what does good posture look like?'),
    ('5d52e7a2-9f5c-5463-852d-b5912e1bcc87', 'OyK0oE5rwFY', 13, 113379, 121120, 'From the side, the spine should have three curves: one at your neck, one at your shoulders, and one at the small of your back.'),
    ('558f848d-d55e-53e3-a236-f66f4e1d8f08', 'OyK0oE5rwFY', 14, 121120, 123433, 'You aren''t born with this s-shaped spine.'),
    ('039342b8-6e2e-5c73-950c-6ec0be4087b8', 'OyK0oE5rwFY', 15, 123433, 126889, 'Babies'' spines just have one curve like a "c."'),
    ('eca3c97c-c797-5b6c-b6a4-b128eb004d6b', 'OyK0oE5rwFY', 16, 132777, 139356, 'These curves help us stay upright and absorb some of the stress from activities like walking and jumping.'),
    ('ce2dfadf-fa4b-5242-996f-6524dea9fd23', 'OyK0oE5rwFY', 17, 139356, 142047, 'If they are aligned properly, when you''re standing up,'),
    ('39e2a7d2-70be-52cd-a67f-cfd100b807ba', 'OyK0oE5rwFY', 18, 142047, 147763, 'you should be able to draw a straight line from a point just in front of your shoulders, to behind your hip,'),
    ('2416b1e7-3e84-51a1-9326-6f297fb15a87', 'OyK0oE5rwFY', 19, 147763, 152294, 'to the front of your knee, to a few inches in front of your ankle.'),
    ('7a90c5fa-aab6-5567-b133-472e1a3430a5', 'OyK0oE5rwFY', 20, 152294, 156048, 'This keeps your center of gravity directly over your base of support,'),
    ('a093c710-1e24-5f1d-9e7c-c706b530d38a', 'OyK0oE5rwFY', 21, 156048, 160956, 'which allows you to move efficiently with the least amount of fatigue and muscle strain.'),
    ('eeb4e1b6-eb36-53c2-ac58-d3e30a3025ce', 'OyK0oE5rwFY', 22, 160956, 165394, 'If you''re sitting, your neck should be vertical, not tilted forward.'),
    ('ad2e6d87-de10-551c-8215-849fa24bfe62', 'OyK0oE5rwFY', 23, 165394, 169245, 'Your shoulders should be relaxed with your arms close to your trunk.'),
    ('c6eaafe7-a1d4-54da-bfc5-415ac7c3a96b', 'OyK0oE5rwFY', 24, 169245, 173613, 'Your knees should be at a right angle with your feet flat on the floor.'),
    ('361b171a-db57-5427-a03b-1b6e23947290', 'OyK0oE5rwFY', 25, 173613, 176399, 'But what if your posture isn''t that great?'),
    ('360d82e3-4185-5588-b3e6-aab8c9d38c78', 'OyK0oE5rwFY', 26, 176399, 179229, 'Try redesigning your environment.'),
    ('a864a1c0-e3d9-5750-96e3-b3e7e5a1fd8c', 'OyK0oE5rwFY', 27, 179229, 183694, 'Adjust your screen so it''s at or slightly below eyelevel.'),
    ('6e7b39cf-00cb-538f-bb5c-599ab40cf88c', 'OyK0oE5rwFY', 28, 183694, 191462, 'Make sure all parts of your body, like your elbows and wrists, are supported, using ergonomic aids if you need to.'),
    ('e9810443-671e-5713-aa8d-19ee545620b7', 'OyK0oE5rwFY', 29, 191462, 196534, 'Try sleeping on your side with your neck supported and with a pillow between your legs.'),
    ('e7520b0c-ba18-5b1e-a177-d8a360bdf633', 'OyK0oE5rwFY', 30, 196534, 202282, 'Wear shoes with low heels and good arch support, and use a headset for phone calls.'),
    ('b578a038-d6df-5ce0-b725-9d6ba20adc60', 'OyK0oE5rwFY', 31, 202282, 205711, 'It''s also not enough to just have good posture.'),
    ('ecace11c-e063-5453-bf13-32c6de438476', 'OyK0oE5rwFY', 32, 205711, 210147, 'Keeping your muscles and joints moving is extremely important.'),
    ('4eec2aed-c5ba-5ab8-b0e6-95f0b964845e', 'OyK0oE5rwFY', 33, 210147, 218723, 'In fact, being stationary for long periods with good posture can be worse than regular movement with bad posture.'),
    ('6849e963-e427-5a92-8f98-8a6005d64098', 'OyK0oE5rwFY', 34, 218723, 221034, 'When you do move, move smartly.'),
    ('eaae8037-b00c-50ef-bd1d-b14e258483b0', 'OyK0oE5rwFY', 35, 221034, 224030, 'Keep anything you''re carrying close to your body.'),
    ('3cad1db9-93ca-5d20-b89d-c89dd2ef4ff3', 'OyK0oE5rwFY', 36, 234509, 243920, 'Using your muscles will keep them strong enough to support you effectively, on top of all the other benefits to your joints, bones, brain and heart.'),
    ('1628c659-6f2e-52b7-9b45-29a97b9bcc92', 'OyK0oE5rwFY', 37, 243920, 250651, 'And if you''re really worried, check with a physical therapist, because yes, you really should stand up straight.'),
    ('024fed77-244f-52bb-91db-b1d221348d15', 'QBddNulwhKo', 1, 30, 7860, 'Hello and welcome to Real Easy English, the podcast where we have real conversations in easy English to help you learn.'),
    ('8a5e2e6d-a4d3-5150-8de1-3a1ebedf0925', 'QBddNulwhKo', 2, 28746, 34590, 'Actually, I''m really happy today because the Sun is shining, and it''s warm,'),
    ('ddecb592-da8e-5626-96ff-a7096aa2a3eb', 'QBddNulwhKo', 3, 34590, 39350, 'and it seems like it''s been a long time since we had such nice sunny weather.'),
    ('272c7e94-9b6d-5c17-a100-0498378f7edd', 'QBddNulwhKo', 4, 39350, 45190, 'I know, the changing of the seasons is so wonderful, and actually, that''s what we''re talking about today.'),
    ('6ec46df8-2ce1-5a7b-a330-9ba97baee48d', 'QBddNulwhKo', 5, 51771, 57230, 'So in the UK, we – our seasons are roughly like this.'),
    ('00284ca4-487d-5958-8f04-359c65ad606f', 'QBddNulwhKo', 6, 79619, 85310, 'Well, you can probably guess because I''m so happy that it''s spring and summer combined.'),
    ('db90e68f-bdfb-5cba-a805-7d19c644f95d', 'QBddNulwhKo', 7, 85310, 90110, 'So anything with long late nights and evenings I love.'),
    ('46856e5c-03ac-5543-bc50-510d4805e5ce', 'QBddNulwhKo', 8, 90110, 92630, 'What else is good about summer?'),
    ('c465d0c6-baca-5ceb-9128-9c01d8f51a90', 'QBddNulwhKo', 9, 92630, 96790, 'In the summer, you can be outside.'),
    ('48b12138-7890-55a5-b758-2bb254702af9', 'QBddNulwhKo', 10, 96790, 100670, 'You can go swimming in the sea.'),
    ('f3fd70aa-7dad-5487-a9a1-841da6be2fb5', 'QBddNulwhKo', 11, 100670, 106910, 'You can stay up late and you have wonderful light in the UK.'),
    ('6da46fef-7b62-59f2-8583-1760976f5959', 'QBddNulwhKo', 12, 106910, 109230, 'What''s your favourite season then, Georgie?'),
    ('54164d38-5a2c-5a23-958a-018d02d61b5d', 'QBddNulwhKo', 13, 109230, 114430, 'Well, I''m a big fan of the seasons, the transition seasons.'),
    ('ec1fa671-d363-5200-b960-40c3c15e273e', 'QBddNulwhKo', 14, 114430, 119790, 'So I really like spring and autumn, especially spring.'),
    ('e76c95c3-c11e-529e-8b11-b68b27992bb2', 'QBddNulwhKo', 15, 119790, 129812, 'Right now we''re in spring in the UK, and you can see everyone looking happier because we''ve had a really long, hard, dark,'),
    ('a21bf810-3fce-52ec-973a-5dce392bb091', 'QBddNulwhKo', 16, 129812, 135314, 'cold winter and everyone is smiling now because they...'),
    ('777a7942-96ed-579b-9d58-c0105047961e', 'QBddNulwhKo', 17, 135314, 139110, 'there are blossoms on the trees which make me so happy.'),
    ('43cdca9e-d020-5ac6-9ada-9b7bea416c84', 'QBddNulwhKo', 18, 139110, 141830, 'I love seeing pink blossoms on the trees.'),
    ('de2169dc-b454-5f12-a21c-7deaec7c6204', 'QBddNulwhKo', 19, 141830, 148270, 'The days are warmer and, yeah, there''s this sense of a transition.'),
    ('869ac0be-dbf2-5451-b972-8da5a3c093cb', 'QBddNulwhKo', 20, 148270, 150310, 'Same with autumn.'),
    ('1bfbbe8d-5e1f-5e3e-802c-5ea1fae65aa8', 'QBddNulwhKo', 21, 150310, 157070, 'Although you''re leaving the summer months, I really love the colours on the trees as well.'),
    ('b2ef053d-d9ba-59cf-a9e3-e3c557c3942e', 'QBddNulwhKo', 22, 157070, 165550, 'Especially those cooler, crisp days when the sky is blue and the leaves are orange and brown.'),
    ('d71220c4-83b8-5eac-8f28-ba038d2706d2', 'QBddNulwhKo', 23, 165550, 166580, 'I love that.'),
    ('fa5d4fc6-773c-52dd-b25f-7ac2fbca0df6', 'QBddNulwhKo', 24, 166651, 172190, 'You''re making me look forward to autumn, and it''s not even summer yet.'),
    ('ae687fcb-d0f7-56d6-b723-8e62c9a920e2', 'QBddNulwhKo', 25, 172190, 174270, 'Is there a season that you don''t like?'),
    ('bd8e0bb5-86de-510d-823f-161bb76be736', 'QBddNulwhKo', 26, 174270, 176990, 'I do like all the seasons.'),
    ('86b8a5c0-d677-50a7-b4de-14860c25a84e', 'QBddNulwhKo', 27, 176990, 181670, 'I like to have balance, so I wouldn''t like to have summer all year round,'),
    ('62b4b92d-cd60-5c2f-b94a-4d292459c5ef', 'QBddNulwhKo', 28, 181670, 188641, 'but I think winter is my least favourite because of the dark days.'),
    ('aafd96e7-aa35-56c1-a525-88d1ca3e6f54', 'QBddNulwhKo', 29, 188641, 204799, 'In the UK I think it''s particularly hard because, especially January and February, it''s really cold and there''s nothing really to get us through the...'),
    ('04810d8a-a290-5c76-8c99-2a4aa517e766', 'QBddNulwhKo', 30, 204799, 206390, 'the sad times.'),
    ('bbec9dc4-477b-54f6-a88e-f1415c497fd5', 'QBddNulwhKo', 31, 206390, 207790, 'I know exactly what you mean.'),
    ('54c4e1c8-a63f-585e-94c7-c6e1f9960270', 'QBddNulwhKo', 32, 207790, 213339, 'There are good things about winter, but mostly it''s just difficult, isn''t it?'),
    ('3fd7b0d5-58a8-5e50-8334-f78342e7abe5', 'QBddNulwhKo', 33, 213790, 214790, 'It''s the dark.'),
    ('05d39153-b399-5972-b1a4-3fd04d7f781d', 'QBddNulwhKo', 34, 214790, 216060, 'I can''t stand it.'),
    ('42ce76c2-cd62-58c4-a99d-473687bbfc3d', 'QBddNulwhKo', 35, 216364, 222550, 'So, as I said, I quite like having the balance of different seasons throughout the year.'),
    ('2ab64731-6ebb-511d-b9e7-5b747c0d63c8', 'QBddNulwhKo', 36, 222550, 225670, 'I like to have transitions and changes.'),
    ('93fc27ea-5c3e-56c5-a774-38eb7a05be32', 'QBddNulwhKo', 37, 225670, 226750, 'What about you, Neil?'),
    ('06d7e9b6-e6b6-5603-8c45-328ce61e60ff', 'QBddNulwhKo', 38, 226750, 228386, 'How do you feel about...'),
    ('378ebb11-95f8-535e-aadb-4ae648774f1d', 'QBddNulwhKo', 39, 228950, 230990, 'Yeah, I think I agree.'),
    ('411ef3d7-f022-5624-b932-5f40c2455e54', 'QBddNulwhKo', 40, 230990, 241628, 'I mean, it would be nice to have a shorter winter, but I think I would still prefer to have different seasons because, like I said,'),
    ('4ac60031-09ff-5d3c-a77e-247653189235', 'QBddNulwhKo', 41, 241628, 246830, 'I really like the late light evenings in the summer.'),
    ('412cfb07-3080-5ce7-a9c9-e85d7ed177fc', 'QBddNulwhKo', 42, 246830, 251710, 'And I think, even though I hate the dark winters, I would really miss that,'),
    ('279f7c03-3dd0-5e06-b48a-86f3187b71c1', 'QBddNulwhKo', 43, 251710, 257460, 'if the weather was nice all year but got dark at the same time, like at six or seven o''clock.'),
    ('99297c45-b5c4-5f57-b515-e7672d0fd509', 'QBddNulwhKo', 44, 262390, 265910, 'OK, let''s recap the language we heard in the conversation.'),
    ('f6cb6362-3338-59c2-a726-866e6afb7037', 'QBddNulwhKo', 45, 265910, 268750, 'We learned different ways to talk about the seasons.'),
    ('ce31cfe1-3814-52bf-a4d7-4fca92727e35', 'QBddNulwhKo', 46, 268750, 274700, 'For example, ''looking forward to'' – that means you''re excited for something to happen in the future.'),
    ('444407cb-396c-575f-b691-f47525e1c69e', 'QBddNulwhKo', 47, 275313, 281630, 'So I''m really looking forward to the warm, light, sunny evenings in the summer.'),
    ('75657c93-1961-5b36-969a-682bcb1f640c', 'QBddNulwhKo', 48, 281630, 285870, 'We heard ''to be a big fan of'' – that means that you really like something.'),
    ('27a2470a-d840-54b1-b0f0-0ce130e13a09', 'QBddNulwhKo', 49, 285870, 289590, 'For example, I''m a big fan of spring and autumn.'),
    ('47df4e9c-9d84-51b6-bf10-1e4bfbfe4fb6', 'QBddNulwhKo', 50, 289590, 292990, 'Yes, Georgie is a big fan of the transition seasons.'),
    ('23122527-1aa4-5732-b148-307f74a1d034', 'QBddNulwhKo', 51, 292990, 296230, 'I''m not such a big fan of winter, though.'),
    ('d2efa8f3-d06a-538f-b45d-5edd4d421827', 'QBddNulwhKo', 52, 296230, 301350, 'Actually, I can''t stand it, which means that I really hate it.'),
    ('7bd9b5b7-cc7f-5d29-a1f0-f8d0b73fdaad', 'QBddNulwhKo', 53, 301350, 303910, 'Thanks for listening to Real Easy English.'),
    ('518752df-2c7d-5b5d-9e83-bc101a8da20c', 'QBddNulwhKo', 54, 303910, 309190, 'We''ve talked about the seasons in the UK, but the seasons are different all around the world.'),
    ('c262d5d4-67b2-54b2-9d0f-983faf86894d', 'QBddNulwhKo', 55, 309190, 311539, 'What are the seasons like where you live?'),
    ('4d598569-0182-5b6d-bfb5-07c8b14fea6c', 'QBddNulwhKo', 56, 315950, 317500, 'We always like to hear from you.'),
    ('eb85cca6-b6e1-5331-ae7e-1a975ea6b2b4', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 1, 4860, 11638, 'Stanford University - Please join me in welcoming Dr. Atul Gawande.'),
    ('0bc07f4c-cea1-512a-aa94-288958a8ced3', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 2, 29810, 30820, 'Thank you all.'),
    ('89d10f57-82e7-54d6-8e3e-839430e91535', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 3, 30820, 32960, 'Thank you, president Tessa Levine.'),
    ('abacd4b4-5eda-5eb8-94e2-fed2d8e01dd8', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 4, 49440, 58623, 'In may, I celebrated the graduation of my own child from college from Berkeley College of Music, not that Berkeley,'),
    ('5c7e69be-06b0-5c6e-901e-5a4d6f2adc37', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 5, 60280, 63343, 'and it was such a beautiful milestone.'),
    ('ccb8db65-6aa9-5531-aaa0-cb312acf52cd', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 6, 64680, 70100, 'But I have to admit it was deflating to have to mark it from our family room.'),
    ('443ad46d-a9bb-5da7-946a-07a0c84ee233', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 7, 70100, 73693, 'Hunter sat on the couch, in cap and gown,'),
    ('43719206-4662-572c-a0f5-d0dc8b8cfc10', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 8, 74390, 85740, 'watching the virtual ceremony waiting for their name to appear after a tough year of virtual music school without ensembles, without performances.'),
    ('6441d254-e406-5b5f-abf8-ae6c82fe53df', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 9, 100590, 107490, 'The Corona virus has taken millions of people from this planet and it made tens of millions more so sick,'),
    ('00b9adb4-f9db-59b3-aad2-b1a37e90f8ca', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 10, 107490, 110933, 'they had to be in a hospital in order to keep breathing.'),
    ('edda67e6-3a86-5eb0-9199-5706e7ccef5e', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 11, 111780, 121490, 'Those with the least wealth and opportunity, those who couldn''t retreat behind their screens suffered most.'),
    ('e0a263b9-1681-57ad-b8a8-46e6194fb722', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 12, 131820, 135070, 'It shuttered workplaces and schools.'),
    ('b4cfa4ee-8b40-5c62-95cf-af8befbca84d', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 13, 135070, 146783, 'It took away our ability to come together to hear music, to break bread, to hold weddings and funerals, to simply let children play.'),
    ('6108033f-0f64-594c-82d8-b62f4026c8b7', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 14, 148100, 151753, 'It did this for an entire year.'),
    ('efa6bbc2-2ec7-5091-b16b-df30e130ae15', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 15, 152920, 157500, 'For much of the world, the worst is not passed.'),
    ('bc0ebdd6-b10f-5a5f-be6e-86546b34758e', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 16, 165050, 168440, 'We are so lucky to live in this country,'),
    ('f8039fe7-e972-52c4-8ab8-68d0951d2c87', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 17, 168440, 178683, 'which has supplied such remarkably effective vaccines and in such quantities that we''re now giving away hundreds of millions of doses globally.'),
    ('7509c629-2cd8-57b3-bf2b-6dcaea3c22fd', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 18, 187190, 198563, 'Vaccines reached so many people, that against all expectations, we can gather here like this to cheer for you at graduation.'),
    ('03b6279f-f435-58e5-adcc-da129863c1a9', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 19, 208710, 214193, 'I remember my graduation one sunlit day like this years ago.'),
    ('95eaf77f-e29e-5116-b7a2-e054043f678b', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 20, 215020, 219410, 'I remember the joy of precessing into the stadium with my friends.'),
    ('3db750c9-79db-5886-8976-90d40ccfc464', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 21, 219410, 224640, 'I remember scanning the crowd to look for the smiling faces of my family members.'),
    ('1b4ac530-81bc-5d33-8dfe-9086c91019cc', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 22, 224640, 230183, 'And I remember the annoying question everyone asks new graduates.'),
    ('a2d15768-ef2f-54a1-8db8-f514ea775ccb', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 23, 231100, 233023, 'So what now for you?'),
    ('3f711bea-f293-5e8b-84b9-bd8a414a6436', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 24, 234700, 239480, 'And I had an answer, more school.'),
    ('8d21021d-d579-5bb1-856b-9f575a075cc3', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 25, 239480, 247270, 'And your answer might be the same or it might be a job, a trip, a move back home.'),
    ('aad186a6-573e-53b5-92f5-27c6bd36c7df', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 26, 247270, 250993, 'But the truth was that none of us knew what was ahead for us.'),
    ('3d5ecbff-5fac-5a2e-9fa2-24854220874a', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 27, 252780, 254930, 'Really, how could we?'),
    ('8d2427b9-a325-5647-a624-09b914f2fe45', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 28, 264220, 275040, 'For example, I had classmates who''d make their mark helping the people of a post-communist Russia and Eastern Europe, and a post apartheid South Africa,'),
    ('47c7e0a6-5257-5565-ae07-96573cbe9385', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 29, 275040, 278792, 'none of which was more than a fever dream back then.'),
    ('e3aae6f1-f35a-5c3f-aabd-706c9ec21106', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 30, 280090, 296350, 'My tech friends would later take jobs with names that would have been in comprehensible, such as app designer, driverless car engineer, data scientist,'),
    ('29ba6785-a052-5ab9-9d03-ae7fcec14348', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 31, 296350, 306143, 'chief information security officer, blogger, or for that manner, Peloton instructor.'),
    ('ee8e34df-d11e-53da-82a8-bfa6a8c707f9', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 32, 308080, 319283, 'In medicine, friends later worked in unimagined fields like genomics, face transplantation and mRNA vaccine production.'),
    ('a72dad98-e4f1-5ce1-8eef-32f868765292', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 33, 326670, 334940, 'No less fantastical in public health, I have friends who would work to implement the country''s first health reform program to seek universal coverage,'),
    ('4972aaeb-e035-5923-b009-69b78211706c', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 34, 334940, 339160, 'signed into law by America''s first black president.'),
    ('89d56e35-b03b-5e32-853e-ecd6691458d3', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 35, 345090, 351593, 'My classmates would also have personal life experiences that were equally unpredictable, though more familiar.'),
    ('0dd46f7f-0f13-543c-83b4-334189a2c735', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 36, 352980, 354780, 'They''d fall in love.'),
    ('98fa59fe-7048-587a-b70f-6c00bcc98f7e', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 37, 354780, 356760, 'They''d fall out of love.'),
    ('e897d040-5771-5804-affe-4e24364d88df', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 38, 356760, 359660, 'They''d navigate sickness and injury.'),
    ('8105530e-37e5-568f-b25c-9b7ab52d8308', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 39, 359660, 363480, 'They''d grow families and they''d lose family members.'),
    ('27b52c24-1ec6-5151-9c87-72cabc6e99c7', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 40, 363480, 366673, 'A few died way too soon.'),
    ('b0ae86e4-09ae-5f69-829a-cfee86a84a6c', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 41, 368040, 373583, 'What now, is a question you will ask your whole life.'),
    ('db84bc60-d6ac-5472-8179-317d399fe69d', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 42, 374810, 378072, 'Entering medical school, I had a plan.'),
    ('6788473f-70fc-5d72-9157-397f9350f455', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 43, 378780, 380031, 'I liked plans.'),
    ('3e6a2a5d-6ff5-5a8f-91a8-033ef4ddc077', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 44, 380790, 384530, 'I wanted to do public health research and practice medicine.'),
    ('04783802-b2bc-5f5c-90a8-12fb33e094f6', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 45, 384530, 387210, 'So I planned to train in primary care.'),
    ('7647037f-0d20-59c4-a2cd-aa1b1cb0940e', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 46, 387210, 392392, 'The specialty fit these interests, and as a bonus that had the shortest residency program.'),
    ('0714222a-faad-59a4-8e96-a08b0c3df855', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 47, 393840, 399560, 'But then my clinical rotation in surgery upended my tidy scheme.'),
    ('f89f58b7-3634-576d-9c99-0faf79edbf4e', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 48, 399560, 402840, 'What I saw captivated me.'),
    ('83c0272b-821e-5439-ba6b-f089310918fb', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 49, 402840, 409450, 'The sur realness of opening the bodies of living people drew me in, instead of pushing me away.'),
    ('7666e444-3693-5b63-999d-cb39f62289af', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 50, 409450, 416630, 'And so did the surgeons, all of them ordinary, flawed human beings, with imperfect skills,'),
    ('a8b10d70-a7fc-5aa6-908d-24fac2963209', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 51, 416630, 425983, 'incomplete knowledge and yet the confidence to nonetheless act and to take accountability for whatever outcome resulted.'),
    ('2007f125-898e-53ac-ab88-ea8a8e587c62', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 52, 427770, 430843, 'People say in moments like this, follow your passion.'),
    ('2990397f-65ad-5e4e-bfba-fe915eb3a169', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 53, 432080, 434379, 'But how many of you even know what that is?'),
    ('fc393e8a-5525-5a3b-b925-95a01943494b', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 54, 437320, 443893, 'I had my share of enthusiasms, but sitting where you are, I wouldn''t have called any of them my passion.'),
    ('eb0d2258-073c-58d2-8ba9-3ae2876b39f9', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 55, 444590, 449223, 'I had no idea which enthusiasms would endure and which would fade.'),
    ('b071aa1f-6cb9-52fc-a057-8c10e1dc2296', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 56, 449990, 455660, 'Over time, however, I came to be able to tell the difference between the things in merely absorbed me.'),
    ('bb81b399-400a-5cb4-be9d-90d025464edc', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 57, 455660, 462410, 'the way that TikTok videos do now, and things that energized me.'),
    ('f6109ee8-b0e2-5ae2-9041-1e0909669efb', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 58, 462410, 464910, 'Seeing the difference took a while.'),
    ('34a2b257-dcd4-5fb6-b052-6c29aa0034a1', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 59, 464910, 469052, 'Coming to Stanford from rural Ohio was mind blowing.'),
    ('5bbb53e1-0dd8-5bf5-80e2-3cb0efb02b0b', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 60, 469810, 477440, 'It exposed me to a wider range of things to do and to be than I''d known.'),
    ('4a194df8-0f4a-518c-9816-84c23f4adb27', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 61, 485220, 491550, 'A professor gave me a job in his laboratory working on a devastating retinol disease.'),
    ('12f797cb-47f4-5bc0-9f48-f7d009262f41', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 62, 491550, 494140, 'I learned to play electric guitar.'),
    ('57323a68-f6c2-568e-b3e9-02684e41f8fe', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 63, 494140, 497623, 'I volunteered to stuff envelopes for a presidential campaign.'),
    ('6455c4c6-879a-5648-b906-eef3a037c78f', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 64, 499040, 506660, 'Many of these interests came and went but I came to recognize when something truly energized me.'),
    ('2cc0f3af-8ea6-5aa6-bf87-effd2a3e5856', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 65, 506660, 511590, 'The radio show, for example, was not such a case.'),
    ('d1e10d55-2ac0-5eff-9822-20252761d279', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 66, 517190, 526780, 'After two or three shows, the fun of our on-air repartee and championing our latest new wave heroes waned dramatically.'),
    ('ca99f185-0be7-5784-a6bc-848ac048efba', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 67, 526780, 530783, 'I began sleeping in and I totally flaked out on my roommates.'),
    ('88b1d746-0009-5b6a-b149-5454deb94f33', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 68, 531800, 536343, 'On the other hand, I consistently lost time in the lab.'),
    ('afc3f92d-34d9-509f-84e8-8e595e1c404c', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 69, 537210, 541510, 'Likewise, for my late night discussions with my political science friends.'),
    ('1acbdf04-e738-5eff-8998-6b92b462c6ac', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 70, 541510, 548302, 'I ended up taking so many policy and political theory electives that I added a second major to my biology major.'),
    ('d9ce7c46-be5f-5dbd-9c2d-940e47c299c0', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 71, 549020, 557190, 'I wasn''t good at anything yet, but I found a few things I was willing to work at long enough to get better.'),
    ('4e5f3d91-d855-5322-ae77-afaabc09b306', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 72, 557190, 559839, 'And I learned to pay attention when that happened.'),
    ('5ac7b3aa-a8df-5b82-bfd6-54b6f1d90e28', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 73, 561970, 569233, 'More recently, I attended a talk by Dr. Bob Wachter, who now chairs the department of medicine at UCSF.'),
    ('50adf764-a2fd-5045-b83d-4693a8c2a1d2', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 74, 570180, 575710, 'Answering a question from a graduate student seeking advice, he said something that stuck with me.'),
    ('fb374b3e-43f3-57e4-9fa2-d098bf5e05f0', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 75, 585340, 591430, 'And looking back, this was pretty much what I''d done, I''d realized.'),
    ('caf7a939-3cf4-5856-8284-97943b554022', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 76, 591430, 597930, 'In your formative years, you don''t know, you can''t know what will ultimately matter to you.'),
    ('839a22bd-dd43-563c-8daf-4d88b9e2bf39', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 77, 597930, 602583, 'What will grab you by the shoulders and awaken you and stay with you.'),
    ('f306ff22-a875-5a7e-ab59-9197d004ffcf', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 78, 603640, 608680, 'So you have to be open to trying stuff, to saying yes.'),
    ('29f26cf1-c279-5d85-b70e-457b7eb46fc0', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 79, 608680, 613543, 'As you do, pay attention to what fuels you, and what doesn''t.'),
    ('1dec57a1-77d8-5748-91ab-dfa769eae7b3', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 80, 614270, 621750, 'You want to pull apart the experience and figure out specifically what lifted you and what sapped you.'),
    ('1f09adff-f4e6-53ce-8b2d-d551a85223bf', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 81, 621750, 628983, 'And then you want to do all you can to organize your life to do more of the first and less of the second.'),
    ('a5d17d80-9e0b-583f-9fd4-96ce21401dd3', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 82, 630220, 638922, 'With me, for example, I found I was endlessly interested in getting under the surface to understand how the systems we depend on fail,'),
    ('96d04790-7897-58af-81f2-9b2fe78df8d9', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 83, 639780, 647533, 'the flaws of the complex systems inside our bodies, and also inside our society that caused suffering.'),
    ('26fa3854-82b8-5cf5-b007-99865c8dcd1f', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 84, 648260, 657983, 'I had experiences that revealed to me the love of getting my hands in there to tinker with the systems and figure out what was possible to fix.'),
    ('60f5a00e-0563-5e6e-9e8e-ffd3018761f8', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 85, 659120, 661630, 'Knowledge was one thing, but execution was another.'),
    ('9e23643d-2cfc-5856-a4ab-ca45ae0007b1', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 86, 661630, 664320, 'And I found, I cared about both.'),
    ('d89b2469-7043-516b-93ac-79dec94997c6', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 87, 664320, 671060, 'In further experiences, I learned that I love dissembling the story of what happens when people try to fix systems failures,'),
    ('a05911d8-00d5-5084-be60-c51437529386', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 88, 671060, 673903, 'how they succeed and how they don''t.'),
    ('ffb3b3cc-32be-5dc7-a282-2b4ab1c08952', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 89, 674960, 682350, 'For a long time, that meant I was pulled in three directions; to surgery, public health and journalism.'),
    ('2d2ecc41-f8ca-59b8-bafe-2a4e0c820d15', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 90, 682350, 685297, 'Over and over people told me to choose.'),
    ('e7710adc-766b-5a54-a545-2dc1326321e0', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 91, 685297, 687540, '"These things didn''t fit together."'),
    ('e7c42407-6a4d-55a4-8de2-7f660be65e94', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 92, 688690, 691550, 'And for a very, very long time, they were right.'),
    ('03821b6d-abc4-5846-bee5-5d1370fc9114', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 93, 691550, 692920, 'They didn''t fit together.'),
    ('42f1a24f-b0ab-5d99-ad7d-25c35c4f44a2', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 94, 692920, 698182, 'All I saw was that each separately added something that fed me.'),
    ('42f22d9d-dd15-528f-b512-646665b5ec87', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 95, 699360, 702390, 'And eventually each fed the other.'),
    ('453eb32e-4094-5850-896e-50514ede5ff2', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 96, 702390, 708533, 'Surgery showed me the day-to-day reality of illness and our inadequate health systems.'),
    ('5f66eac5-6a07-5094-b7b3-4d21cd1f67cf', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 97, 709260, 713570, 'Writing let me investigate the flaws and ways to address them,'),
    ('a4bff60b-dc77-5bc0-962a-d5ebe8dff0ca', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 98, 713570, 720383, 'and public health training showed me how to design systemic solutions and deliver them at population scale.'),
    ('34577415-3b9a-55f0-87c0-a45f0ff7453b', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 99, 722259, 732093, 'to deliver a team checklist for safer surgery that''s now been adopted worldwide and saved more people from death and disability than car accidents inflict,'),
    ('4071cee1-c178-5353-8b82-193bcdd2b14d', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 100, 733070, 745670, 'or to design a structured conversation between clinicians and patients with serious illness, to ensure that treatment plans incorporate people''s priorities for their lives,'),
    ('3740975c-a249-551e-b0cf-6ac44ee8ee13', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 101, 745670, 747762, 'besides just surviving.'),
    ('4ea085fe-1cfe-5010-bd15-dfe28fc7bbe1', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 102, 749370, 756043, 'Or to build mass vaccination centers and COVID testing programs to help us escape from this pandemic.'),
    ('9187664c-5565-5d59-9779-073e2bcb0587', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 103, 757060, 762673, 'Every few years, I''ve faced a pivotal choice that scared me.'),
    ('1b130ede-7743-5abf-a5d9-5a43e6f2150e', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 104, 764080, 768960, 'One was deciding to train in surgery instead of an internal medicine.'),
    ('1705c85a-70a9-50ce-9804-d4f1b6dbd2a7', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 105, 768960, 773540, 'The training was eight years, instead of three years.'),
    ('79889559-f56f-542e-a307-2d061cb3f065', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 106, 773540, 781120, 'My wife, Kathleen, we met here at Okada house, was pregnant with our first child.'),
    ('d8ffcc40-d344-5329-8fff-808a97dcea7e', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 107, 781120, 785350, 'Surgery was not a natural cultural fit for me.'),
    ('c2d0b10b-8279-5d72-933f-5e445effe1a7', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 108, 785350, 794370, 'My mentors in public health thought the direction was baffling, but still there have been that poll during three months on service.'),
    ('99250c71-e3db-54cf-a76b-71198cac6064', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 109, 794370, 797560, 'So I told myself that I could transfer out if it didn''t work.'),
    ('3ea7bbe1-a18b-57ee-8ac8-56207d8c3a27', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 110, 797560, 799913, 'And I said yes to surgery.'),
    ('bd2c7236-103d-59b2-b0fd-5de8e36410fb', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 111, 801480, 804440, 'Three years later, I also said yes to writing.'),
    ('d6bda0f0-7758-547a-ace9-51184d6df265', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 112, 804440, 807248, 'Yes, a blog on the side.'),
    ('d955bbb3-96f9-5656-8b26-67653c019b06', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 113, 808450, 812830, 'And then during a two year research period with only light clinical duties,'),
    ('e7fa1a4a-4712-5a47-aec3-4b716c9d4f10', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 114, 812830, 818270, 'I said yes to a chance to write longer pieces for the New Yorker Magazine.'),
    ('d9f2f8d8-5a55-56dd-9182-bb1ec809c9b3', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 115, 818270, 825650, 'A few months after I returned to full hospital duties, a publisher offered me the chance to expand those pieces into a book.'),
    ('e317ba58-70b6-5dfd-8038-6fa4fdffa85b', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 116, 825650, 832432, 'And I remember the day at the hospital that I said yes into the phone and accepted the contract.'),
    ('8f4863f8-a97d-51a8-8307-5f312e0df5ed', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 117, 833210, 839230, 'It was later when I got home that night- It was late when I got home that night.'),
    ('4e0e62b9-6694-5828-8835-86411c590138', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 118, 839230, 843500, 'I have three children by then and they were asleep upstairs.'),
    ('77c2b177-b1ba-5b7d-a7bd-62764cad5a43', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 119, 843500, 850120, 'And suddenly, I was flat on my back in a panic on the living room floor.'),
    ('23548c4b-f969-5fc7-9904-59456ce4a1a7', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 120, 850120, 853062, 'What did I just commit to doing?'),
    ('88236811-c5cd-5a9d-8eb3-40bb7e07604b', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 121, 853760, 858333, 'How in the world was I going to deliver during residency?'),
    ('04bc48f7-846a-5fa4-89ea-2bcb64d2b4e4', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 122, 859420, 860970, 'Kathleen, my wife,'),
    ('ba6e3669-1c09-598a-baa2-84672485f5d4', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 123, 874420, 877410, 'So I stilled my pounding heart.'),
    ('69f27b95-5012-57c4-86b0-8245e9c79fa5', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 124, 877410, 885023, 'I kept making time for what energized and motivated me and kept trying to remove time from what beat me down.'),
    ('6eae8f53-621b-54d5-ab41-1a7d149381e2', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 125, 885710, 895432, 'And this meant doing things that didn''t fit with my plan or the images that others had of me, but I never regretted it.'),
    ('ffc712af-8b43-5336-b3f5-78bfbdc2cf49', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 126, 896560, 905663, 'I''ve had great luck and privilege just to have the opportunities I''ve had, like even trying to do surgery or to write.'),
    ('5eb2e012-6c0f-5e11-8f8f-383543a6222d', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 127, 906520, 914553, 'Simply by being in this community, you too have had choices and exposures that few others have.'),
    ('bbc41d6e-7f6f-5466-b11e-092f64b2b654', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 128, 915470, 919363, 'Most people face far tighter constraints on their life.'),
    ('018ebb33-74ef-5c17-9f03-24148d1cb248', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 129, 920900, 930670, 'But I''ve seen that even patients facing the end of life, the tightest constraint of all, have had room to assert their priorities in their lives,'),
    ('c07cb956-61b9-57d5-a0cb-ce1e81114bcf', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 130, 930670, 938862, 'besides just living longer to maximize time for what lifts them up and to try to limit what brings them down.'),
    ('8ab44025-31cf-5dd5-9a76-d0f2adc4fbb1', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 131, 948400, 956090, 'By that, he meant, that by that age, you should know enough about yourself, but what really matters, to you to focus on that.'),
    ('6c96b5f8-7e5c-54fb-bb0e-0dd8390ef075', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 132, 956090, 959743, 'In fact, you have to say no to focus on that.'),
    ('7e920b41-bbe8-5fac-9f35-e1656f1ef895', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 133, 960760, 964110, 'As you get older, this will become your advantage.'),
    ('417bfef7-3880-56f5-93d3-719a010a68e6', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 134, 964110, 975790, 'You begin to know yourself, your capabilities, your gaps, what motivates you well enough to commit to efforts that can run a long time to realize,'),
    ('f992c646-09d7-541d-ab80-a4eecc34a6d4', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 135, 975790, 978280, 'years, decades, if necessary.'),
    ('aa88ffe5-f486-5b79-b23d-327dedf04370', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 136, 978280, 983543, 'You even become willing to work for goals that will not be achieved in your lifetime.'),
    ('77504787-65ad-5a58-91ae-8ac04467df35', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 137, 985840, 988233, 'I want to return to COVID for a moment.'),
    ('c71b2f2d-04be-5a02-92e1-5ce4a9325e5e', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 138, 989590, 993290, 'This plague forced us all to see our lives anew.'),
    ('86beb049-164c-525c-a9bd-f7ec93e553dc', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 139, 994580, 998670, 'Under crisis, we had to pair our lives down.'),
    ('5a648fe1-e3e4-5a80-b8f2-18df1e8c1d61', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 140, 998670, 1001732, 'We had to jettison what could be jettisoned.'),
    ('6259d84f-57a5-5a07-969d-1b760a7511ca', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 141, 1002820, 1005940, 'And we had to keep what truly mattered.'),
    ('56d6fd07-c09b-58d8-bad2-49c71bce5640', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 142, 1005940, 1008790, 'We had to try living in new ways.'),
    ('68027651-9edb-569a-8d5a-e695bf24cf04', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 143, 1008790, 1011810, 'We had to figure out how to endure.'),
    ('e139b5b8-69ba-505e-b09e-63f156552c8a', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 144, 1011810, 1016280, 'For me, dealing with the uncertainty was the hardest part.'),
    ('cc54060a-8778-500e-bffe-042eb34d3e94', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 145, 1016280, 1019040, 'How long would this plague last?'),
    ('e0ceee00-25fb-57db-9792-78baa5000085', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 146, 1019040, 1021130, 'How bad would it get?'),
    ('7100ee52-e745-553b-8290-c2ca641e9618', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 147, 1021130, 1028483, 'What troubled me most though was, the fact that so much of the uncertainty was human made, instead of virus made.'),
    ('7c91c60f-dbe4-5978-89fd-eff10179c123', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 148, 1029360, 1033690, 'The pandemic was and it still is a spreading fire.'),
    ('6d3c7ff2-f6a1-58ec-bbe2-62ea294795e0', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 149, 1033690, 1038630, 'Experts actually figured out, rather quickly, how to stop it.'),
    ('0103b73b-d04e-52a9-91dd-beea162aa138', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 150, 1038630, 1048440, 'With wide testing, masks, avoiding indoor crowds, use of good ventilation and ultimately with vaccination.'),
    ('f2bae71f-c2c7-5b0a-b1ba-d39bc21ec005', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 151, 1048440, 1052023, 'But knowledge is one thing, and execution is another.'),
    ('0b67352e-a98c-52a3-bb53-b247deb64f17', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 152, 1052740, 1060213, 'Those communities that came together across political lines, take knowledge of the threat and fight the fire, were able to stop the fire.'),
    ('011def4c-5d85-5ed7-86cf-0ab52df91659', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 153, 1061080, 1063092, 'Our nation did not come together.'),
    ('f59bf44a-0829-5567-946a-cc176cc1a6d1', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 154, 1063810, 1072420, 'The fact that we could not collectively summon the commitment required, that we''ve had key leaders who saw political opportunity and undermining that commitment,'),
    ('fd541a31-a504-5848-bc95-a9ce7eb084d1', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 155, 1072420, 1075323, 'has been distressing beyond words.'),
    ('bb1bc399-6427-5170-8357-907d4f351ae9', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 156, 1076510, 1078230, 'Leaders have a choice.'),
    ('4dfa0661-cc30-5418-b22d-0af70a1b181e', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 157, 1078230, 1086572, 'They can move ahead by driving division and stoking fear or they can move ahead by binding us together and confronting our fears.'),
    ('b94ddc1b-4f58-557b-b902-1cc29ebf8034', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 158, 1087360, 1094880, 'The divisive path generates attention more easily and generates more immediate gratification.'),
    ('31e4ff9a-bef4-5387-8c41-adb81502a04e', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 159, 1094880, 1098592, 'That means we''ll always have those who will take the divisive path.'),
    ('9f9c6c62-3f3e-5983-b166-244614e49b4f', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 160, 1099360, 1106863, 'The fact that that path is ultimately dispiriting for people, however, while the other path raises our spirits up,'),
    ('492f2fc5-ef40-5945-bd44-3a178e0830f5', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 161, 1107640, 1111763, 'gave me confidence about which eventually would prevail.'),
    ('5b4ce307-699f-52ce-ae0c-6c0aae278f1e', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 162, 1113150, 1124240, 'That confidence has been shaken to be sure but we stand here together today because enough of us have come together across political lines and increasingly across countries,'),
    ('8d7f0193-c7ed-51f3-adbf-dc5314cb840b', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 163, 1124240, 1127683, 'to take up the vaccines and fight the fire.'),
    ('f387c66f-00ab-5964-8b49-bfa5de953eb6', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 164, 1130430, 1150110, 'The difference between- The difference between these two paths is worth remembering as we each encounter that what now question in our lives.'),
    ('1bedb6cd-3750-5a75-8a82-914cfa80bb4a', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 165, 1150110, 1153723, 'That question about what we individually will commit to next.'),
    ('858b2a1b-1625-5515-bae0-ff0325fae4f7', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 166, 1154440, 1164210, 'All of us are seeking how to express our worth and everyone does have worth, equally with everyone else''s human beings,'),
    ('e6ab1100-84d4-59f8-88f7-b5f91913518d', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 167, 1164210, 1167523, 'we do just by being here in this world.'),
    ('759fa81f-51e9-5982-8773-73b5858670df', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 168, 1168280, 1174610, 'To discover how to express that worth, you just have to keep saying yes until you found it.'),
    ('223ce186-2719-54c0-a7cd-3a12daf4c5ac', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 169, 1174610, 1176609, 'And if you do that, you will find it.'),
    ('258cb2fc-168f-5464-bfc4-f223e18f57f9', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 170, 1177650, 1182110, 'But the better choices are not often the easiest or most enjoyable ones.'),
    ('071aa17a-9b5d-59f5-9208-dd655115c74c', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 171, 1182110, 1186780, 'The most meaningful goals are usually slow to achieve.'),
    ('13d5e4d5-0743-5f9b-ba5e-8a3737cce6b9', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 172, 1186780, 1192630, 'They''re also usually the ones that bind people together rather than push them apart.'),
    ('0ba6a017-ac69-57c3-8d21-856db658d5c8', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 173, 1192630, 1196970, 'That feeds not only your purposes, but feeds their purposes.'),
    ('dc73a93b-3d06-577a-9713-48144a700845', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 174, 1196970, 1202100, 'For it turns out that the beautiful secret of how our species is made,'),
    ('1690b2e7-009e-5920-bfd3-03dec1db5673', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 175, 1202100, 1207883, 'is that we are often most energized when we help others express their worth.'),
    ('1078b7f2-1a6c-5140-ac1e-615a2187e450', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 176, 1209880, 1214340, 'That truth is easy to miss behind our screens.'),
    ('a8f7b140-de3a-5082-8fb7-15c76f68d849', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 177, 1214340, 1218173, 'watching the news, when separated from one another.'),
    ('8580be41-7a10-57a4-be16-c15708475e11', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 178, 1219060, 1228693, 'But it is the reason why we all, all of us here have gathered and why we hold such confidence in you.'),
    ('069c911b-a771-51b4-9d2c-e65235c50ae6', 'S7HCEtsEeJA', 179, 1230730, 1239692, 'And this truth is why we believe you and your entire generation are the reason our better angels will prevail.'),
    ('4763a503-0e3d-53ca-b014-c40d23b72b00', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 1, 30, 3830, 'Hello and welcome to Real Easy English.'),
    ('fd013ea3-154e-5156-b3bb-b35aba3b7648', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 2, 3830, 9459, 'In this podcast, we have real conversations in easy English to help you learn.'),
    ('6cbd5c1c-b5d0-50ae-94aa-269e4cf624f2', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 3, 17270, 20500, 'where you can also find a free worksheet.'),
    ('c41442f5-9795-598f-909d-9a923b98866e', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 4, 37579, 40430, 'And I did some other interesting things too.'),
    ('89449eb6-0389-517b-8a56-a42298f7c7fe', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 5, 50580, 55710, 'So tell us about your boring day, by the sound of it.'),
    ('38f12cb1-461f-5c4d-b43b-4df6546d4c1a', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 6, 55710, 61750, 'So it was a prison museum about, like, medieval England.'),
    ('2f9f435a-1e10-544d-a090-e312abf6e4ab', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 7, 61750, 71230, 'So I feel like it could have been a bit more exciting, but instead I was reading a lot about religion and kings and stuff.'),
    ('958eba72-1d97-500a-bcd2-2eb53295e7c9', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 8, 71230, 76819, 'OK, so you spent your weekend learning about prisoners from the Middle Ages?'),
    ('5c6d7750-a7e1-5e18-9f7a-656891b420e4', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 9, 78750, 83540, 'I wouldn''t recommend it too much, but museums can be a good...'),
    ('0b627d03-539e-5dfc-8fc4-cb7da95d67f3', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 10, 88100, 90219, 'I used to go on lots of day trips with my kids.'),
    ('d3914844-9e74-5a00-805c-ff5878a3b59a', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 11, 91470, 96870, 'So, fun things to do, we''d go to the seaside in the summer.'),
    ('27c25098-875e-5c54-8dc7-0dd3d62c5f65', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 12, 96870, 100500, 'But they don''t really want to hang around with me anymore.'),
    ('509472f9-bdec-56bd-9225-1ec8b7fd2846', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 13, 100647, 101910, 'You''re not cool.'),
    ('a255952a-3f5f-5db4-92d5-82dfaf92af63', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 14, 101910, 103660, 'I''m on my own.'),
    ('9f7b90cb-3853-5ff6-b9eb-f1561dda9d05', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 15, 103660, 108630, 'Yeah, so I like watching sport.'),
    ('1fcba18a-138e-51c9-bfdc-e0551423b20a', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 16, 108630, 111710, 'So I might meet friends and go and watch sport.'),
    ('7a4a9052-068a-555c-a73c-f55c8eae2c14', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 17, 111710, 115699, 'On Friday, I spent most of the day watching a cricket match.'),
    ('f569f8f8-58b3-5113-b221-2e91553474ba', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 18, 115870, 117780, 'That sounds like a good day out.'),
    ('812d89c2-94b2-520c-bff5-d11679218bb6', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 19, 118043, 126270, 'Well, actually, I did go to a museum, but, I also went to the theatre this weekend and that was a really enjoyable day trip.'),
    ('051e0210-b3e3-5aa8-b6a9-3c3b17237ff2', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 20, 126270, 128670, 'Did you do any sightseeing?'),
    ('c45d6041-662c-5cdd-a39e-abbe0e17f85e', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 21, 128670, 135310, 'Well, yeah, we walked past quite a lot of famous sights, so we went past Big Ben.'),
    ('1750f32b-190c-55ca-b7c0-e07cdff9376b', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 22, 135310, 138590, 'We walked past the London Eye, Trafalgar Square.'),
    ('14e64eb6-e35e-5e5a-a09b-d11677346a8d', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 23, 138590, 140550, 'Yeah, we did a lot of walking.'),
    ('6d99b56c-cfde-5b05-be9c-450c9c145a73', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 24, 140550, 142350, 'I''m quite tired, actually.'),
    ('a5b5ba35-e50e-5717-a5ff-2318240eae56', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 25, 142350, 145430, 'And are you a thrill seeker?'),
    ('3b98ee79-fe38-57dd-9f9b-e4a23707703d', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 26, 145430, 151030, 'So do you like really adventurous day trips?'),
    ('daf391e7-a35f-5683-acc6-671917635caf', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 27, 151030, 159060, 'Like, do you like parachuting or bungee jumping or any of those things or roller coasters?'),
    ('4ab3acc0-251c-595a-9362-fc6300558479', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 28, 160310, 164990, 'I would say no, not really.'),
    ('46b860ac-0638-5d49-9f46-16377d75d46e', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 29, 164990, 168670, 'I think if I''m on holiday, I''m a bit more adventurous.'),
    ('17b68dd3-5c3a-5944-8acd-c5a4a3f103ef', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 30, 168670, 177390, 'So I''ve done things like, you know, been in speedboats and that kind of stuff, which I find quite enjoyable.'),
    ('8160f716-fc7e-508a-a675-a97778cde38e', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 31, 177390, 179790, 'If I''m, if I''m abroad it tends to be.'),
    ('228a01a0-1f41-5234-a5e3-554511e89213', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 32, 179790, 188340, 'But I don''t really like roller coasters and that sort of thing because they, they scare me and make me feel a bit sick.'),
    ('7e5dd138-4fa8-5cf2-8902-53158afcfe56', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 33, 188500, 192230, 'So I wouldn''t go to a theme park for a day out.'),
    ('789440b0-0130-56e4-b70d-dca94df48d3c', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 34, 192230, 193338, 'What about you?'),
    ('440f6fa4-1cc9-5f5b-8523-04fb87a7863e', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 35, 193338, 195220, 'Are you a thrill seeker?'),
    ('f4353e03-6480-5496-a223-d30486bb0bdc', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 36, 196170, 202421, 'I used to like theme parks when I was younger, but I don''t really like them anymore.'),
    ('55176f46-0cad-53ff-a89a-856eb04efe12', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 37, 202830, 209350, 'So is there anywhere that you have always wanted to visit for a day trip, but you haven''t?'),
    ('133981f0-cde3-5076-b88b-940ac2409cc9', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 38, 209350, 211849, 'There is actually.'),
    ('a8247e42-b531-5676-a65d-27cab851f944', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 39, 213430, 218790, 'I went to Brighton when I was a child, but I can''t remember it at all, to be honest.'),
    ('79dc842d-7d7b-5319-b980-1a7d8a7d2d93', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 40, 218790, 222550, 'So I''d really like to go there on a day trip because it''s not too far.'),
    ('577c4613-d813-5763-99d0-6a7b5112c435', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 41, 222550, 226350, 'And I like the beach and I want to have an ice cream.'),
    ('bc277be3-7836-5f27-888e-eb1b1bbca234', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 42, 226350, 227830, 'Maybe some fish and chips.'),
    ('3b30d489-a4bc-58fb-9b1a-fac968481ef9', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 43, 227830, 229179, 'I used to live in Brighton.'),
    ('b213e2fc-fd2f-5a25-a52e-af1ef97f639f', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 44, 230710, 232870, 'You can take me on a day trip and show me around.'),
    ('a153277f-0571-5482-a9d5-c634882e5ba8', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 45, 232870, 234550, 'I definitely think you should visit.'),
    ('e5bcd43f-e61f-59ce-9a4c-776c2926c544', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 46, 234550, 235710, 'How about you, Neil?'),
    ('60a9e1b6-dd4f-5cee-841e-c11f06013a89', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 47, 235710, 239700, 'Is there anywhere that you''ve always wanted to go on a day trip?'),
    ('9495c7bb-8d21-55f0-9c90-077b377d620a', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 48, 240277, 250110, 'I really like train travel, and London is actually really close to the rest of Europe, but we have the sea in the way.'),
    ('5c6d3d8e-c8e9-5cf5-887e-99679a9c94af', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 49, 250110, 255830, 'But we have the tunnel, so we can, we can go to Paris, just for the day.'),
    ('0542ca0a-04f8-572f-8de6-304798ad7d24', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 50, 255830, 263830, 'And I, it seems like maybe, like it''s not long enough to just to go somewhere like Paris for a day, but you can do it.'),
    ('22d41132-d297-5399-b896-54ec07b9c89c', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 51, 263830, 270710, 'And I kind of like that idea of just going from London to Paris for the day and back on the train.'),
    ('d9c59892-2c0f-5e24-93e7-eaa5eddc0d13', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 52, 270710, 271990, 'Sounds a bit crazy.'),
    ('dc74f471-6ff2-5061-b38b-d3962f5aa933', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 53, 271990, 274030, 'You''d need a really early train.'),
    ('bf335a44-9127-56c5-b20e-e2fb64b4a88c', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 54, 274030, 278780, 'Really early train, really late train back and lots of energy.'),
    ('ba2b31b8-a2e0-5956-af1b-db306ede34ac', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 55, 279950, 281980, 'You wouldn''t need to pay for your accommodation.'),
    ('abddc2f1-09cf-5bb4-a0f0-3d5a7d0c10aa', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 56, 282630, 286300, 'Go up the Eiffel Tower, come back down, go home.'),
    ('a2eeb42b-b77b-5af6-84d7-51dc52f084f1', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 57, 292270, 296390, 'Let''s recap the vocabulary we heard during the conversation.'),
    ('814d65d7-a198-5c1e-8b39-debf3e8370de', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 58, 296390, 300710, 'We had ''day trip'', which means visiting a place for just the day.'),
    ('3dec8450-f928-5260-ac9f-6135c57469fe', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 59, 300710, 307110, 'We heard ''thrill seeker'', which describes someone who takes part in risky and exciting activities.'),
    ('bc242894-775b-5d42-941c-989b1cd104b5', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 60, 307110, 310430, '''Adventurous'' means ''unusual and exciting''.'),
    ('bf4aa69a-2236-57ab-85d8-6a15d790fd68', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 61, 310430, 319230, 'A person can be adventurous, or an experience or a day trip can be adventurous, like Neil''s trip to Paris.'),
    ('b51b0c69-3cab-523b-bc45-dceeb4b97d93', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 62, 319230, 328550, 'We used the word ''sightseeing'', which describes the activity where you walk around looking at famous buildings and monuments.'),
    ('d91a5b0a-5d41-5f57-affe-81655e7659d1', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 63, 328550, 332659, 'And that''s it for this episode of Real Easy English.'),
    ('2cb6e227-8509-5c21-8586-5d231bfb95ea', 'S7mfygW40Cs', 64, 339110, 341910, 'And we''ll be back with more easy conversations soon.'),
